# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/), read by
# GitHub's "Cite this repository" box and by Zenodo's GitHub integration when
# a release is archived. `version` and `date-released` are deliberately
# omitted: Zenodo takes both from the release itself, and a hand-maintained
# copy here would only drift (RELEASING.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use punchmark, please cite it as below. Report the package version AND
  the rulings-spec version your rulings were produced under (`punchmark env`
  prints both): a rulings-spec change means a recorded measurement meaning
  changed.
title: "punchmark: a retrospective producer identifier for hosted LLM routes"
abstract: >-
  punchmark consumes archived benchmark response text (no logprobs, headers or
  timing) and returns a producer-identity ruling per (route, window):
  SAME-PRODUCER, SUBSTITUTED or UNDETERMINED at a caller-declared false-alarm
  rate, calibrated on same-route within-window resamples and cross-fitted
  nulls, with seeded-substitution power analysis reporting the minimum
  substituted fraction the archive could have resolved. It emits a one-line
  certificate attachable to a published score and an append-only,
  content-addressed rulings store gated in CI. Every verdict is closed-set and
  certifies the route label as served. It says nothing about model weights and
  makes no statement about the quality of any model.
type: software
